  "details": "<p>G\u00f6bekli Tepe was enrolled as a UNESCO World Heritage site on 1 July 2018.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The site of G\u00f6bekli Tepe, located in the Germu\u015f mountains of south-eastern Anatolia, was the location of a Neolithic hilltop sanctuary. This sanctuary, thought to be a series of stone enclosures with T-shaped pillars carrying carving of wild animals, was built in the Pre-Pottery Neolithic and ranges in date from 9,600 to 8,200 B.C.",
